---
Ledgers: agent-safe accounting

Usage: ledgers [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  serve              Start the native Ledgers server
  completions        Generate shell completions
  mcp                Serve MCP over stdio, relaying to the server with your agent key
  demo               Demo company operations
  accounts           Commands under `ledgers accounts`
  agreements         Commands under `ledgers agreements`
  allocation-rules   Commands under `ledgers allocation-rules`
  approval-settings  Commands under `ledgers approval-settings`
  approvals          Commands under `ledgers approvals`
  audit              Commands under `ledgers audit`
  bank               Commands under `ledgers bank`
  bills              Commands under `ledgers bills`
  company            Commands under `ledgers company`
  connections        Commands under `ledgers connections`
  documents          Commands under `ledgers documents`
  entries            Commands under `ledgers entries`
  fiscal-years       Commands under `ledgers fiscal-years`
  groups             Commands under `ledgers groups`
  invoices           Commands under `ledgers invoices`
  keys               Commands under `ledgers keys`
  numbering          Commands under `ledgers numbering`
  parties            Commands under `ledgers parties`
  periods            Commands under `ledgers periods`
  reports            Commands under `ledgers reports`
  subledger          Commands under `ledgers subledger`
  tax-settings       Commands under `ledgers tax-settings`
  units              Commands under `ledgers units`
  help               Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Output machine-readable JSON
      --profile <NAME>  Profile name (default: from LEDGERS_PROFILE or 'default')
      --url <URL>       Server URL (overrides LEDGERS_URL and the profile)
  -h, --help            Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version         Print version

Ledgers is not tax or legal advice. Check rates and returns before you file.
